        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/e68b1a/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-09-06T00:34:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>p 28 'Events (and Fear) Work Differently than Powers'</p>\n<p>If you voluntarily Destroy Presence to prevent Blight being&nbsp;added to a board, that Presence could be saved by Flowing and Silent Forms Dart By (Shroud of Silent Mist) or Hold the Island Fast with a Bulwark of Will&nbsp;(Stone’s Unyielding Defiance).</p>\n<p>p 28 'Presence: Returning, Removing, Replacing, Destroying'</p>\n<p>(Removal is generally voluntary) and interaction&nbsp;with other effects: a few Powers can save Presence from Destruction but not Removal.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>i think rulebook say&nbsp;'presence destroy prevent effect is prevent&nbsp;even&nbsp;voluntary destroy effect' and 'a few Powers can save Presence from Destruction but not Removal. Removal(presence)&nbsp;is generally voluntary(destory presence).</p>\n<p>q1.voluntary destroy is not remove?&nbsp; i need more explain 'a few Powers can save Presence from Destruction but not Removal.'</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>q2. when land would be ravage or building, rampant`s 'choke the land with green's destroying presence + ' flowing and silent forms dart by'&nbsp; can prevent destroying? (result, that land do not ravage action / build action, and rampant`s presecent not destroyed.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:54:15.524Z",
