      {
        "id": 233709,
        "name": "dpt",
        "username": "dpt",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-09-06T03:16:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>On Q1: \"destroy\" can be voluntary or not, but in any case is different from \"remove\". It only counts as \"remove\" if it literally uses that word, as on a card like the Major power Bargains of Power and Protection. A power like the two you mention (Flowing and Silent Forms Dart By or&nbsp;Hold the Island Fast with a Bulwark of Will) can prevent anything that says \"destroy\" (like Draw Down into a Consuming Void), but not something like Bargains of Power and Protection.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Q2: Yes, you can prevent the Ravage by (attempting to) Destroy Presence, then prevent the Destruction with&nbsp;Flowing and Silent Forms Dart By.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:09:36.607Z",
